{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/928139-worst-rpg-book-designs","id":928139,"title":"Worst RPG book designs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-08T08:08:19-07:00","id":928139,"title":"Worst RPG book designs","content":"What it says on the tin. What are those books who have really bad design for reading or whatever? A friend recently reminded me of Trinity (formerly known as Aeon) back in the day... <a href=\"http://imgur.com/s61Soae\" target=\"_blank\">http://imgur.com/s61Soae</a> Seriously, light yellow on bright white pages? Then again, it was the 90s... It was the style. Like onions on belts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:10:46-07:00","id":928415,"title":"","content":"Depends on bad for what.<br /> <br /> Cyberpunk v3.0 will always hold a place in my heart for the artwork. Specifically it looked like someone stuck their arm in a silver-painted flexible dryer vent, took a photo and called it cyberpunk.<br /> <br /> Ex2, Shadowrun 4, and Anima: Beyond Fantasy will always hold a special place for their mechanics. The painfully bad mechanics.<br /> <br /> While not as bad, Star Wars saga edition holds memorable note for the droids and jedi, both of which were easily broken.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mutants and masterminds 3e holds special mention, because while the game is fairly solid, it's the first time I encountered a SRD that was far more readable and clear in communication than the book itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T10:18:42-07:00","id":928797,"title":"","content":"When they put in numerous side pages and text quote boxes on a page to the point where it breaks up and distracts you from the main subject you are trying to read. Eclipse Phase I am looking at you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T13:00:05-07:00","id":928876,"title":"","content":"Are we talking artwork or specifically covers? If we're talking covers, anything with a cheesecake cover instantly gains a special place in my heart of shame. In terms of WoD books, Immortals stands out as having a really horribly cheesy cover. And while it isn't a book, Bloodlines is probably the single worst videogame cover I've ever seen. It's a perfect storm of everything that makes a cover bad- bad art, sexualization, having little to no relation to what the game's actually like...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T15:57:14-07:00","id":928927,"title":"","content":"I meant more than just covers. But also just design like text. Like light yellow text on bright white pages for the headers. This makes them headache inducing to read. But yeah, cheesecake covers definitely count. I think the worst I can think of is Exalted's Savant and Sorcerer (I think that was the name) with... I have no clue. <a href=\"https://imgv2-1-f.scribdassets.com/img/document/192030809/original/5ec8a87137/1464729085\" target=\"_blank\">https://imgv2-1-f.scribdassets.com/i...137/1464729085</a> Seriously, that's pretty bad. And doesn't even make any sort of sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T17:09:33-07:00","id":928964,"title":"","content":"For me it's Eoris and it's character sheets. <a href=\"http://i42.tinypic.com/20uzp87.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Behold</a>.<br /> <br /> It's like a WoD character sheet mixed with a SAT and some kind of ancient summoning ritual. I don't want to fill in that character sheet and accidentally call a Shoggoth to our world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T17:28:02-07:00","id":928976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/928139-worst-rpg-book-designs?p=928876#post928876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we talking artwork or specifically covers? If we're talking covers, anything with a cheesecake cover instantly gains a special place in my heart of shame. In terms of WoD books, Immortals stands out as having a really horribly cheesy cover. And while it isn't a book, Bloodlines is probably the single worst videogame cover I've ever seen. It's a perfect storm of everything that makes a cover bad- bad art, sexualization, having little to no relation to what the game's actually like...</div> </div> </div> </div>To me the most awful cover i have had the displeasure to see have been<br /> <br /> Werewolf the forsaken: The pack. Which is weird because while leblanc cover is an awful that gives me flashback to CoG tribebook revised the interior art of leblanc is pretty good but man he dropped the ball to center of the earth on the cover<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://d.gr-assets.com/books/1463022874l/30173319.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://d.gr-assets.com/books/1463022874l/30173319.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://d.gr-assets.com/books/1463022874l/30173319.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://d.gr-assets.com/books/1463022874l/30173319.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Shadowrun 5th data trails.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/2216/150001.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/2216/150001.jpg</a><br /> <br /> And we cant have a discussion about horrible covers without honorable mention of dark phoenix publishing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/darkphoenix/images/3/30/Mage.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20120910021108\" target=\"_blank\">http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/...20120910021108</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T04:13:21-07:00","id":929176,"title":"","content":"If you want bad covers, check out any from Slasher Flick. I like the games but the Art...Well a picture is worth a thousand words..<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.rpgnow.com/images/2340/147420.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T11:57:03-07:00","id":929306,"title":"","content":"Dark Phoenix is one of those cases where it's so bad that it loops back to brilliant. I would proudly display a shelf full of Dark Phoenix books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T11:57:17-07:00","id":929307,"title":"","content":"Good lord what's wrong with her abdomen. And her right leg. And her right arm. And what's wrong with her faaaace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","user":"Beriorn","date":". 07-10-2016, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:02:57-07:00","id":929312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/928139-worst-rpg-book-designs?p=928964#post928964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it's Eoris and it's character sheets. <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://i42.tinypic.com/20uzp87.jpg&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Behold</a>.<br /> <br /> It's like a WoD character sheet mixed with a SAT and some kind of ancient summoning ritual. I don't want to fill in that character sheet and accidentally call a Shoggoth to our world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good god, is that a HYBRID character sheet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:10:52-07:00","id":929319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/928139-worst-rpg-book-designs?p=929307#post929307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good lord what's wrong with her abdomen. And her right leg.And her right arm. And what's wrong with her faaaace.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Her left arm too. I thought it looked off, and when I tried putting my arm in that position, it's a very unnatural seeming one. Especially to defend yourself or attempt it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T13:43:51-07:00","id":929369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/928139-worst-rpg-book-designs?p=928415#post928415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ex2, Shadowrun 4, and Anima: Beyond Fantasy will always hold a special place for their mechanics. The painfully bad mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god, Anima... I bought the book because my friends and I all loved the art. Then I tried reading it... 3 tables to resolve a single attack? Re-rolling Initiative every round? I had to tell my friends there was no way I'd be able to run a game that would be any kind of fun using this system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:41:15-07:00","id":929477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/928139-worst-rpg-book-designs?p=929369#post929369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh god, Anima... I bought the book because my friends and I all loved the art. Then I tried reading it... 3 tables to resolve a single attack? Re-rolling Initiative every round? I had to tell my friends there was no way I'd be able to run a game that would be any kind of fun using this system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had a similar experience with my group. One player bought the book because it looked cool.<br /> <br /> I read it because it looked cool, but didn't even understand how to build a character after about 30 minutes reading so I put it down to read later... and once I finally did find time to read and digest all of it, I told the group a few basic things about it - like how ranged attacks have a cap on the bonus that can be added to the attack roll after all modifiers are applied so that an arrow is only ever so hard to dodge - and all but one of the group were immediately convinced there would be no fun to be had in playing it (the singular player that didn't agree likes having a lot of crunch to fiddle with and track in video games, so he said &quot;It might be kinda cool, maybe&quot; because he'd love a video game that ran on those rules but isn't sure he'd enjoy it on paper).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T19:13:46-07:00","id":929494,"title":"","content":"Two suggestions for this thread:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.thebadguyswin.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.thebadguyswin.com</a> carries on the work of Something Awful's incredible WTF, D&amp;D? column, tearing apart terrible RPG books with hilarious commentary.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying Public Radio has a podcast they do through their Patreon called RPPR After Hours where they buy awful 80s and 90s games and then lose their minds. They also do another podcast called WoD The Heck where they introduce a newbie to the worst of oWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T21:53:18-07:00","id":929551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/928139-worst-rpg-book-designs?p=929477#post929477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had a similar experience with my group. One player bought the book because it looked cool.<br /> <br /> I read it because it looked cool, but didn't even understand how to build a character after about 30 minutes reading so I put it down to read later... and once I finally did find time to read and digest all of it, I told the group a few basic things about it - like how ranged attacks have a cap on the bonus that can be added to the attack roll after all modifiers are applied so that an arrow is only ever so hard to dodge - and all but one of the group were immediately convinced there would be no fun to be had in playing it (the singular player that didn't agree likes having a lot of crunch to fiddle with and track in video games, so he said &quot;It might be kinda cool, maybe&quot; because he'd love a video game that ran on those rules but isn't sure he'd enjoy it on paper).</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually went ahead and had a game that lasted several sessions. <br /> <br /> Setting aside the painful mechanics as a general game running sort of thing, the balance was the issue... we started at level 9 or 10. We had an acrobat that was hard to hit, and bounced around the battlefield. An Emo Knight that was depressed over the things he had done in the past and was a solid fighter. And then we had a psyonicist who had a pet floating island, and a magic character that rebuilt and enhanced himself to the point that a minor attack was calling down a kingdom destroying swarm of meteors which he could do effortlessly and continually. Just slight amount of class capability difference in the way the grand canyon is a small divot in the ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T08:06:03-07:00","id":929743,"title":"","content":"I tried to read Deliria and got nowhere. Every other page was on a completely different topic, often contradicting the material on the previous page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}